# Loaded by `npm test` (node --env-file). Many test files import routes/chat.js,
# which opens the conversation database as soon as it is imported. The test
# runner starts those files in parallel processes, and on a fresh checkout they
# all tried to create and initialise the same server/data/memory.sqlite at once
# ("database is locked"). An in-memory database per process means no test
# touches the disk and none can collide. Variables already set in the
# environment, and the values in a developer's own .env, do not override this.
SQLITE_PATH=:memory:
